cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "szl-cram: classical energy reasoning with certificates"
message: >-
  Szl-cram solves constraint-satisfaction problems with a hand-set
  Hopfield-style energy and ships a machine-checkable energy certificate
  on every answer. If you use the engine, datasets, or the audit results,
  please cite this software and the CRAM paper it audits.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lutar
    given-names: Stephen
    email: stephen@szlholdings.com
    affiliation: SZL Holdings
repository-code: "https://github.com/szl-holdings/szl-cram"
abstract: >-
  Pure-numpy reimplementation, receipt-bound audit, and honest reproduction
  of CRAM (arXiv:2611.17309): Hopfield-Tank pairwise constraint energies for
  Sudoku-class reasoning, pseudolikelihood training, focused-Gibbs and
  mean-field anneal search, an energy-certificate format for governance,
  and a Cloudflare Worker edge solver. Includes the decoy-minima finding:
  positives-only PL fits create spurious deep minima at solution depth
  (min off-diagonal cost -0.5506).
keywords:
  - hopfield-networks
  - constraint-satisfaction
  - energy-based-models
  - sudoku
  - machine-learning-reproducibility
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-17"
